GAL22V10
C68CPU

; Processor PCB U7 pins 1-12. Pin 12 is ground, not R/W.
PHI2 RW VMA A15 A14 A13 A12 A11 A10 A9 A8 GND
; Pins 13-24. The select outputs are physically active low.
NC NC NC NC NC NC BUSOK IOSELN BANKSELN ROMSELN RAMSELN VCC

; Valid bus cycle: both phase 2 and VMA are high.
BUSOK = PHI2 * VMA

; Express the inactive-high selects directly. This keeps GALasm's
; output polarity unambiguous and matches the board net names.
; RAM       $0000-$BFFF
RAMSELN = /PHI2 + /VMA + A15 * A14

; Banked RAM $C000-$DFFF
BANKSELN = /PHI2 + /VMA + /A15 + /A14 + A13

; I/O       $E000-$E0FF
IOSELN = /PHI2 + /VMA + /A15 + /A14 + /A13 + A12 + A11 + A10 + A9 + A8

; ROM       $E100-$FFFF
ROMSELN = /PHI2 + /VMA + /A15 + /A14 + /A13 + /A12 * /A11 * /A10 * /A9 * /A8

DESCRIPTION
C68 processor address decoder. Pin 2 is the unused R/W input; pin 18 is
unused. Pins 19-23 drive BUS_OK, /IO_SEL, /BANK_SEL,
/ROM_SEL and /RAM_SEL respectively.
